  "dom_id": "step-40259",
  "name": "Perpendicular Lines",
  "problem": "Two lines are **perpendicular** if they intersect and form a $90^\\circ$ angle. \n\nFor example, the lines $r$ and $s$ below are perpendicular.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/73d2e836e942d6e468c8d9652921a9321b842d47b54ba59529123da61a9a96b4.png)\n\nWhen two lines are perpendicular, we can express this with the symbol $\\perp,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr \\perp s\n$$\n\nIn words, we say, \"the line $r$ is perpendicular to the line $s$.\"",
